    "The unit is named after Hertz, the German physicist who studied electromagnetic waves.",
    "One thousand hertz means one thousand cycles per second, and it can also be written as one kilohertz, or kHz.",
    "The wave on screen is a one thousand hertz tone; it completes each cycle in one thousandth of a second.",
    "The frequency is set by the vibration of the source; it does not change even when sound passes into another medium."
